</tex-math></inline-formula> is a hyperparameter controlling the influence of this term, the proximal term ensures that local models do not diverge significantly from the global model, which can be crucial when clients have non-iid data.</p></div><div class="section_2" id="sec4f"><h3>F. Initialize Global Model</h3><p>A global CNN model is initialized with a set of initial weights, typically set randomly or using pre-trained weights from a similar task. This model serves as the baseline for federated training and will be iteratively updated based on client contributions.</p></div><div class="section_2" id="sec4g"><h3>G. Federated Training for R Rounds</h3><p class="has-inline-formula">The training process is executed over <i>R</i> rounds, following these sub-steps:
</p><ol><li value="1" data-list-item-label="1."><p><b>Distribute Global Weights to Clients</b>: The global model weights are sent to each client, allowing them to start training from the same baseline.</p></li><li value="2" data-list-item-label="2."><p class="has-inline-formula"><b>Local Training at Client</b><inline-formula class="inline-formula"><tex-math notation="LaTeX"><span class="MathJax_Preview" style="display: none;"></span><span class="MathJax" id="MathJax-Element-9-Frame" tabindex="0" style=""><nobr><span class="math" id="MathJax-Span-217" style="width: 0.54em; display: inline-block;"><span style="display: inline-block; position: relative; width: 0.43em; height: 0px; font-size: 124%;"><span style="position: absolute; clip: rect(1.349em, 1000.39em, 2.374em, -1000em); top: -2.204em; left: 0em;"><span class="mrow" id="MathJax-Span-218"><span class="mi" id="MathJax-Span-219" style="font-family: MathJax_Math-bold-italic;">i</span></span><span style="display: inline-block; width: 0px; height: 2.204em;"></span></span></span><span style="display: inline-block; overflow: hidden; vertical-align: -0.077em; border-left: 0px solid; width: 0px; height: 1.004em;"></span></span></nobr></span>
</tex-math></inline-formula>: Each client <i>i</i> trains its local model on its dataset using the FedProx loss function defined earlier. This involves updating the model weights based on local data and minimizing the FedProx loss over several epochs:<disp-formula id="" class="display-formula"><tex-math notation="LaTeX"><span class="MathJax_Preview" style="display: none;"></span><div class="MathJax_Display" style="text-align: center;"><span class="MathJax" id="MathJax-Element-10-Frame" tabindex="0" style="text-align: center;"><nobr><span class="math" id="MathJax-Span-220" style="width: 16.831em; display: inline-block;"><span style="display: inline-block; position: relative; width: 13.548em; height: 0px; font-size: 124%;"><span style="position: absolute; clip: rect(1.284em, 1013.44em, 2.751em, -1000em); top: -2.258em; left: 0em;"><span class="mrow" id="MathJax-Span-221"><span class="msubsup" id="MathJax-Span-222"><span style="display: inline-block; position: relative; width: 1.167em; height: 0px;"><span style="position: absolute; clip: rect(3.364em, 1000.69em, 4.148em, -1000em); top: -3.978em; left: 0em;"><span class="mi" id="MathJax-Span-223" style="font-family: MathJax_Math-bold-italic;">Ï‰</span><span style="display: inline-block; width: 0px; height: 3.978em;"></span></span><span style="position: absolute; clip: rect(3.498em, 1000.45em, 4.145em, -1000em); top: -4.329em; left: 0.718em;"><span class="texatom" id="MathJax-Span-224"><span class="mrow" id="MathJax-Span-225"><span class="mi" id="MathJax-Span-226" style="font-size: 70.7%; font-family: MathJax_Math-bold-italic;">r</span></span></span><span style="display: inline-block; width: 0px; height: 3.978em;"></span></span><span style="position: absolute; clip: rect(3.326em, 1000.36em, 4.145em, -1000em); top: -3.652em; left: 0.718em;"><span class="texatom" id="MathJax-Span-227"><span class="mrow" id="MathJax-Span-228"><span class="mi" id="MathJax-Span-229" style="font-size: 70.7%; font-family: MathJax_Math-bold-ital