        </p></div><div class="section_2" id="sec4i"><h3>I. Plot Metrics Across Rounds</h3><p>To visualize the global model performance over training rounds, metrics are plotted. This helps in identifying trends and the effectiveness of the FL approach in training the model</p></div><div class="section_2" id="sec4j"><h3>J. Deploy Final Model</h3><p>After completing the federated training over R rounds, the final global model is ready for deployment.</p><p class="has-inline-formula">The <b>Federated Averaging (FedAvg)</b> algorithm is a commonly used technique in FL, particularly useful for collaboratively training a global model across multiple parties while securing data privacy. In the context of <b>BTC</b>, FedAvg ensures that a central server coordinates training without requiring clients to share their sensitive MRI data. The process works as follows:
</p><ol><li value="1" data-list-item-label="1."><p>A local model is trained on a separate subset of data by each client.</p></li><li value="2" data-list-item-label="2."><p>Once a communication round is complete, the clients send their locally trained model weights to the server.</p></li><li value="3" data-list-item-label="3."><p>The server then aggregates the updates by averaging their weights to get a new global model, which is then distributed back to the clients for the next round of training.</p></li><li value="4" data-list-item-label="4."><p class="has-inline-formula">Mathematically, if <inline-formula class="inline-formula"><tex-math notation="LaTeX"><span class="MathJax_Preview" style="display: none;"></span><span class="MathJax" id="MathJax-Element-22-Frame" tabindex="0" style=""><nobr><span class="math" id="MathJax-Span-668" style="width: 1.508em; display: inline-block;"><span style="display: inline-block; position: relative; width: 1.183em; height: 0px; font-size: 124%;"><span style="position: absolute; clip: rect(1.373em, 1001.18em, 2.698em, -1000em); top: -2.204em; left: 0em;"><span class="mrow" id="MathJax-Span-669"><span class="msubsup" id="MathJax-Span-670"><span style="display: inline-block; position: relative; width: 1.167em; height: 0px;"><span style="position: absolute; clip: rect(3.364em, 1000.69em, 4.148em, -1000em); top: -3.978em; left: 0em;"><span class="mi" id="MathJax-Span-671" style="font-family: MathJax_Math-bold-italic;">Ï‰</span><span style="display: inline-block; width: 0px; height: 3.978em;"></span></span><span style="position: absolute; clip: rect(3.498em, 1000.45em, 4.145em, -1000em); top: -4.329em; left: 0.718em;"><span class="texatom" id="MathJax-Span-672"><span class="mrow" id="MathJax-Span-673"><span class="mi" id="MathJax-Span-674" style="font-size: 70.7%; font-family: MathJax_Math-bold-italic;">r</span></span></span><span style="display: inline-block; width: 0px; height: 3.978em;"></span></span><span style="position: absolute; 