</tex-math></inline-formula> is the total number of clients, the key idea behind FedAvg is that the global model learns from the diverse data distributions across clients, resulting in a model that generalizes well without the need for centralized data storage. This is particularly beneficial for tasks like brain tumor classification, where medical data privacy is critical. However, FedAvg assumes that all clients contribute equally and does not explicitly handle situations where clients have heterogeneous (non-IID) data distributions, leading to potential issues when data across clients varies significantly.</p></li></ol><div class="algorithm rule-both" id="alg1"><h3>Algorithm:</h3><div class="alg-item label"><span class="label">2)</span><p>Step 1: Dataset Preparation and Initialization</p></div><div class="alg-item"><p><i>Load and Pre-process Data:</i></p><p><i>Load the brain tumor MRI dataset</i></p><p class="has-inline-formula"><i>Resize images to</i><inline-formula class="inline-formula"><tex-math notation="LaTeX"><span class="MathJax_Preview" style="display: none;"></span><span class="MathJax" id="MathJax-Element-28-Frame" tabindex="0" style=""><nobr><span class="math" id="MathJax-Span-739" style="width: 5.272em; display: inline-block;"><span style="display: inline-block; position: relative; width: 4.247em; height: 0px; font-size: 124%;"><span style="position: absolute; clip: rect(1.431em, 1004.2em, 2.441em, -1000em); top: -2.258em; left: 0em;"><span class="mrow" id="MathJax-Span-740"><span class="mn" id="MathJax-Span-741" style="font-family: MathJax_Main;">128</span><span class="mo" id="MathJax-Span-742" style="font-family: MathJax_Main; padding-left: 0.222em;">Ã—</span><span class="mn" id="MathJax-Span-743" style="font-family: MathJax_Main; padding-left: 0.222em;">128</span></span><span style="display: inline-block; width: 0px; height: 2.258em;"></span></span></span><span style="display: inline-block; overflow: hidden; vertical-align: -0.094em; border-left: 